A||||7||fierospeeder||Fiero production has ended!||||9||
Z||000000||fierospeeder||12-20-2001||04:49 AM||||Ive went through 6 years of hot rod magazines and found this small cliping.  I will post more stuff that i found on the fiero that ive read in the early years.<P>Hot rod magazine  November 1988<P><BR>"Fiero production has ended with the last '88 Fiero rolling off the line and the plant shut down.  With sales of only 24,000 units in 1988, the Fiero dropped more than 43% even though the '88 model was a terrific performance car in every respect."||||reg||9
Z||000001||fierospeeder||12-20-2001||05:09 AM||||HOT rod magazine Sept  1983<P>Fiero Facts<P>Pontiac's new Fiero is one of the most exciting new releases for '84.  It is already a superb handler and the 92hp 4 cylinder engine has enough steam to move the car smartly.  Update plans call for a 2.9 liter v6 in '85, and an all-aluminum turbocharged v6 for '86.  Anyone purchasing an '84 fiero wont be disappointed, and with all the super duty equipment available from pontiac and the aftermarket, they'll be able to do some serious Fiero hot rodding immediately.  We also suspenct that Super Duty engines may eventually be certified for the car.  The stuff is too good to leave on the shelf.<P><BR>NOTE  V6 ALUMINUM  TURBO ENGINE||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierospeeder||12-20-2001||05:20 AM||||Hot rod march 1984<P><BR>Upgraded Fiero Performance<P><BR>With the availability of special offroad hardware for the 2.5l fiero powerplant, many fiero owners are already eyeing substantial performance gains.  Pontiac is one step ahead of them by working out an emissionized Super Duty engine package for possible release in 1985 cars.  The basic change involves the addition of the Super Duty cylinder head with larger valves and bigger ports, a special throttle body injection unit combined with a performance computer chip and a performance camshaft.  This package would put the Fiero engine in the 120 hp range which is where it should have been when the cars were introduced.  Ah, but these things take time and Pontiac is moving ahead as quickly as possible.  A few years down the road, you just might be able to purchase a 200 hp super duty fiero right off the show room floor.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierospeeder||12-20-2001||05:25 AM||||Jan 1985  hot rod<P><BR>1985 fiero  gt specs<P>8.5:1 compression<BR>140 net hp @5200 rpm<BR>170 ft-lbs @3600 rpm<P>4 speed manual<BR>final drive ratio 3.65:1<P>2735lbs curb weight<BR>10.2 gallons<BR>18mph city, 22 highway<BR>8.25 sec  0-60mph<BR>16.0 @85.86 mph  quarter mile<BR>.81g skidpad<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierospeeder||12-20-2001||05:37 AM||||HOT ROD January 1984<P>Fiero Alloy v6 CANCELLED<P><BR>Pontiac recently announced that the 2.9L aluminum V6 being developed for the new Fiero is being shelved indefinitely.  They say it's BECAUSE THE CAR WOULD ACTUALLY BE TOO FAST, but that doesn't wash since the 2.8l Chevrolet iron V6 is still being planned for the 1985 model.  It's more than likely a case of INTERDIVISIONAL LOBBYING AND EXPENSIVE, TEMPORARILY INSURMOUNTABLE ENGINEERING PROBLEMS THAT WOULD ADD DRASTICALLY TO THE COST OF THE CAR.  Since Pontiac has successfully launched their 4-cylinder Super Duty engine program, they're counting on its strength to carry the car's performance image.||||reg||1
Z||000005||The Fieromaster||12-20-2001||11:34 AM||||What about WHY it was cancelled....<BR>Insurance prices - yea right, Mr2 survived!<BR>OR was it that the NEW all aluminum 800lbs space frame combined with a ALL new look AND a WICKED new engine in the 89 (we have all seen pics... if not i got a crap load and can show yall) cause the car to OUTPERFORM gm's little baby the Corvette!!??!!<BR>Comon GM cant have a car that STARTED OUT as a COMUTER car become their TOP sports car, specially if it was AFFORDABLE to everyone... It would have to be a more expensive car that they started off using as their namesake car... cough... cough.. corvette.. cough... cough!!!<BR>Hell, Scott has a VIDEO of some IMPORTANT peeps speeking the same thing i JUST did!<P>HEY... HONESTLY before you flame me... THINK about it!  Lighter, more powerful, NEW NEW looks (specially for 89), YOU ALL know what a Fiero can do if we mod ours up a BIT... Just think what the 89 could do then tell me im lying... I KNOW some of the autocrossers in here have taken out NEWER vettes just by adding springs and anit-roll bars (sway bars)!!<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">        <FONT COLOR="red"><B>"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT></B>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">   <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thefieromastersig.gif">     <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AOL IM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="green">1992 Mitsubishi Eclipse GS ~ soon will be turboed</FONT><BR></B><p>[This message has been edited by The Fieromaster (edited 12-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fierokid87||12-20-2001||07:17 PM||||Yep Craig is right about the fact the Vette was threatened by the little Pontiac.  Oh God forbid the Fiero out performs the Vette (not that a few out there already do)  I have the video craig was talking about and its a proven fact that the Fiero was beating out the vette in acceleration, and handling.  <P>Scott<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="red"> Fierokid's  Web site:</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="white">http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero</FONT><P><FONT COLOR="blue">AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierokid.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||LoW_KeY||12-20-2001||09:56 PM||||Yeah go figure.. I was reading the 30th anniversy Trans-am did 163 governed.. wonder why? pretty good that its gone now too.. I've heard rumors they might bring it back later down the road.<P>I can only say GM had some dumb people working for them.  Sure numbers might have been low but for god sakes car sales can slump for awhile then jump.  I read somewhere on the forum they only sold 23,000 vettes in 88.  They can't even tell when they have a good car on their hands.<P>Enough of that.. I could go on and on but it won't do no good, but I am happy they don't make the fiero anymore because everyone would have'em.  Just fustrates me to think what they could've had.  It'll be interesting to see what this POS is that they bring out, because so far the Avalanche/Aztec make me want to puke  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>------------------<BR>AIM: FierFormula88   <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/low_keysig.gif"> ||||reg||1
